    "features": [
      {
        "name": "Glamour",
        "level": 1,
        "scale": 0,
        "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">You can Cast Spells using Influence.</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Spells: </strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">You learn 4 Spells. You learn 1 other Spell every 2 Levels hereafter.</span></p><p><br></p><p><b><strong style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Mana:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> Your Max Mana is equal to (4 × your Level), and the highest amount of Mana you can spend to Cast a Spell is equal to (2 + your Level).</span></p>"
      },
      {
        "name": "Tap",
        "level": 1,
        "scale": 0,
        "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">You gain the Vehement Magic Perk (p. 73), and you can spend your HP as Mana, which also reduces your Max HP by the same amount until</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">you Rest. If you die from this reduction, the Cast still resolves and your body is vaporized.</span></p>"
      },
      {
        "name": "Spell Slinger",
        "level": 2,
        "scale": 0,
        "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The damage die of your Spells is one size larger.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Further, the roll required for you to Crit on Cast Checks and Saves against Casts is reduced by 1, and is reduced by 1 more every 6 Levels hereafter.</span></p>"
      },
      {
        "name": "Quickening",
        "level": 4,
        "scale": 0,
        "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">You can skip your Move to Cast a Spell. You can’t upcast this Casting.</span></p>"
      },
      {
        "name": "Spell Twinning",
        "level": 6,
        "scale": 0,
        "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">If you Cast the same Spell twice on a Turn, the second Cast Check is Favored.</span></p>"
      },
      {
        "name": "Overpowered",
        "level": 10,
        "scale": 0,
        "description": "<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">When you Cast, you can choose to gain 2 Fatigue. If you do, you regain Cd6 Mana at the start of your Turns, and your Cast Max is doubled during the countdown.</span></p>"
      }
    ]
